          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Milwaukee and Makita are both platforms you can stay with for decades. <strong class="text-white">Milwaukee</strong> is the stronger choice for trades that rely on its specialty tools and for buyers who want maximum torque and a 5-year tool warranty. <strong class="text-white">Makita</strong> is the stronger choice for all-day comfort and for the widest range of tools and yard equipment on one 18V battery.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Make the decision on the tools you will actually buy, not on brand reputation, and once you choose, stay with that battery. Switching platforms costs more than the difference between two good brands.
          </p>
